{%- comment -%}
  Mobile pill-tabs treatment is scoped to the v2-style PDPs:
    • handle dtf-transfers              (legacy main DTF PDP)
    • handle dtf-transfers-by-size-v2   (template by-size-tabs-v2)
    • handle dtf-transfers-by-size-v3   (template by-size-bg-options)
  All three share this snippet AND the v2 mobile look — text-only
  pills, no Studio tab, light-blue active fill. The `.dtfut--v2` class
  drives every difference; the CSS itself lives in
  assets/dtf-upload-tabs.css.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign dtfut_v2 = false -%}
{%- if product.handle == 'dtf-transfers' or product.handle == 'dtf-transfers-by-size-v2' or product.handle == 'dtf-transfers-by-size-v3' -%}
  {%- assign dtfut_v2 = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign picker_forced_type = 'bysize' -%}
{%- assign picker_tag_string = product.tags | join: ',' | downcase -%}
{%- if product.template_suffix contains 'gang-sheet' or product.handle contains 'gang' or picker_tag_string contains 'gang' -%}
  {%- assign picker_forced_type = 'gangsheet' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Gang sheets only accept ONE design per cart item (each gang sheet is
  its own product), so multi-select doesn't make sense — disabling
  allow_multi forces the picker into single-select-with-replace mode
  (toggleDesignSelection: selectedDesignIds = [sid]).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign picker_allow_multi = true -%}
{%- if picker_forced_type == 'gangsheet' -%}
  {%- assign picker_allow_multi = false -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign ds_url = b.designStudioUrl | default: '/pages/design-studio' -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Per-tab gates. Every PDP that hosts an upload box wraps it in dtfut,
  but not every product offers Create with AI or Design Studio. These
  flags let the parent (section / block) opt OUT of either tab so the
  pill bar only shows what's actually supported by that product.

  Default: SHOW both tabs (matches the dtf-transfers historical
  behavior). Override by passing `show_ai_tab: false` and/or
  `show_studio_tab: false` to the snippet, OR by setting
  block.settings.show_ai_tab / show_studio_tab to false in schema.
  Section-level overrides (`section.settings.show_ai_tab` etc.) also
  work for sections that don't have block-scoped settings.

  Falsy detection: any of `nil`, `false`, blank string disables the
  tab; anything else (true, "true", missing) keeps it visible.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign show_ai_tab = true -%}
{%- assign show_studio_tab = true -%}
{%- if show_ai_tab_override == false or show_ai_tab_override == 'false' -%}
  {%- assign show_ai_tab = false -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if show_studio_tab_override == false or show_studio_tab_override == 'false' -%}
  {%- assign show_studio_tab = false -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if b.show_ai_tab == false -%}{%- assign show_ai_tab = false -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if b.show_studio_tab == false -%}{%- assign show_studio_tab = false -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if section.settings.show_ai_tab == false -%}{%- assign show_ai_tab = false -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if section.settings.show_studio_tab == false -%}{%- assign show_studio_tab = false -%}{%- endif -%}

